From: OpenAI <noreply@openai.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: enable hardware forward path for active mesh routes

mac80211 only exposes ndo_fill_forward_path through the 802.3 hardware
encapsulation netdev ops, and ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward_path() only
resolves AP/AP-VLAN/station peers. 802.11s mesh therefore cannot hand an
active next-hop peer to drivers such as mt7996, even though mt7996 already
implements net_fill_forward_path() and can translate an associated peer to
a DEV_PATH_MTK_WDMA path with the correct WCID.

Keep the normal mesh datapath and control traffic unchanged. Expose the
forward-path callback on the regular data netdev as well, and only resolve
mesh unicast destinations that already have an active HWMP route. For a
proxied destination behind a mesh portal, resolve the MPP entry first and
then the active path to that portal. If no stable route/next-hop exists,
return to the existing software path without starting route discovery or
changing mesh state.

This allows bridge/PPE flow offload to reuse mac80211's current mesh route
selection while preserving software handling for non-offloaded traffic.

---
 net/mac80211/iface.c | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

--- a/net/mac80211/iface.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/iface.c
@@ -940,6 +940,10 @@ static int ieee80211_netdev_setup_tc(str
 	return drv_net_setup_tc(local, sdata, dev, type, type_data);
 }
 
+static int ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward_path(struct net_device_path_ctx *ctx,
+					      struct net_device_path *path);
+
 static const struct net_device_ops ieee80211_dataif_ops = {
 	.ndo_open		= ieee80211_open,
 	.ndo_stop		= ieee80211_stop,
@@ -948,6 +952,7 @@ static const struct net_device_ops ieee8
 	.ndo_set_rx_mode	= ieee80211_set_multicast_list,
 	.ndo_set_mac_address 	= ieee80211_change_mac,
 	.ndo_setup_tc		= ieee80211_netdev_setup_tc,
+	.ndo_fill_forward_path	= ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward_path,
 };
 
 static u16 ieee80211_monitor_select_queue(struct net_device *dev,
@@ -1035,6 +1040,40 @@ static int ieee80211_netdev_fill_forward
 
 		sta = sta_info_get(sdata, sdata->deflink.u.mgd.bssid);
 		break;
+#ifdef CONFIG_MAC80211_MESH
+	case NL80211_IFTYPE_MESH_POINT: {
+		struct mesh_path *mpath, *mppath;
+
+		/* Hardware flow offload must only consume a route that HWMP has
+		 * already resolved. Route discovery and all mesh control traffic
+		 * remain on the normal software datapath.
+		 */
+		if (is_multicast_ether_addr(ctx->daddr))
+			goto out;
+
+		mpath = mesh_path_lookup(sdata, ctx->daddr);
+		if (mpath && (mpath->flags & MESH_PATH_ACTIVE)) {
+			sta = rcu_dereference(mpath->next_hop);
+			break;
+		}
+
+		/* A bridged client behind the remote mesh node is represented by
+		 * an MPP entry. Resolve its portal first, then reuse the active
+		 * mesh path to the portal to obtain the actual wireless peer.
+		 */
+		mppath = mpp_path_lookup(sdata, ctx->daddr);
+		if (!mppath)
+			goto out;
+
+		mpath = mesh_path_lookup(sdata, mppath->mpp);
+		if (!mpath || !(mpath->flags & MESH_PATH_ACTIVE))
+			goto out;
+
+		sta = rcu_dereference(mpath->next_hop);
+		break;
+	}
+#endif
 	default:
 		goto out;
 	}
